{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>He founded</b> — He mentioned the firmament, the clouds, and the wind; now he mentions the earth." "<b>And the meaning of 'He founded'</b> — for it is set in the height of the heavens and established according to its nature by the power of HaShem; therefore it shall not be moved, for it has no motion, since all of it is small, like a point on a sphere relative to the heavens."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:07.360353341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}